    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42213" root="وقح" body-key="w">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقِحٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقَاحٌ</span></b>  (tropical:)  A man <i>having little shame.</i>
(S, A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقَاحُ الوَجْهِ</span>, an epithet applied to a
woman, (S,) without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>, as well as to a man,
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الوَجْهِ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقِيحُ</span></b> , applied to a man, (tropical:)  <i>Hard-faced,
having little shame;</i> (TA;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقْحَى</span></b> 
applied to woman. (Msb.)

